1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,414
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:15,505
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,555 --> 00:00:18,403
The Little Ghost Who Was Scared of People!

7
00:00:22,955 --> 00:00:27,572
Once upon a time, there was an
old blue house full of windows,

8
00:00:27,622 --> 00:00:29,327
high on top of a hill.

9
00:00:29,651 --> 00:00:33,185
At the very top, it had an attic
with a little round window,

10
00:00:33,235 --> 00:00:34,926
like a curious eye.

11
00:00:35,594 --> 00:00:40,808
One autumn afternoon, a girl named
Lara and her mom came to live there,

12
00:00:40,858 --> 00:00:42,786
carrying moving boxes.

13
00:00:43,430 --> 00:00:47,275
In the tree beside the house
lived Popcorn the little owl,

14
00:00:47,430 --> 00:00:50,011
who knew every corner of that hill.

15
00:00:50,584 --> 00:00:51,960
Hoo, hoo!

16
00:00:52,071 --> 00:00:55,280
How lovely to have new
neighbors around here!

17
00:00:55,330 --> 00:00:57,369
Popcorn said happily.

18
00:00:58,037 --> 00:01:01,298
Lara liked the house, the
garden, and the little owl.

19
00:01:01,652 --> 00:01:03,510
But she had a secret:

20
00:01:03,572 --> 00:01:06,347
she was a tiny bit afraid of the dark.

21
00:01:06,977 --> 00:01:11,927
When night came, the house grew very
quiet, and all you could hear was the

22
00:01:11,977 --> 00:01:13,849
clock in the living room.

23
00:01:14,016 --> 00:01:18,972
Lara was almost asleep when she heard a
strange noise coming from the ceiling.

24
00:01:22,284 --> 00:01:27,254
She opened one eye, then the other,
and pulled the blanket up to her nose.

25
00:01:27,929 --> 00:01:31,962
And then came some very light
little footsteps, walking up above,

26
00:01:32,012 --> 00:01:33,212
in the attic.

27
00:01:36,076 --> 00:01:38,706
Popcorn, did you hear that noise up there?

28
00:01:38,756 --> 00:01:41,294
Lara whispered very quietly.

29
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:43,290
Hoo, hoo...

30
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:45,074
I heard it too.

31
00:01:45,199 --> 00:01:48,746
It sounds like someone is
tiptoeing around up there,

32
00:01:48,796 --> 00:01:52,557
Popcorn answered, her eyes wide open.

33
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:55,808
Lara curled up under her blanket.

34
00:01:56,061 --> 00:01:59,808
The noise stopped, and the
house was silent again.

35
00:02:00,884 --> 00:02:03,862
But what Lara didn't know
was that, up in the attic,

36
00:02:03,912 --> 00:02:06,840
someone else was trembling with fear too.

37
00:02:07,498 --> 00:02:13,287
It was Boris, a tiny, round little
ghost, as white as moonlight.

38
00:02:13,984 --> 00:02:17,926
Boris had lived in the
attic for many, many years.

39
00:02:18,257 --> 00:02:21,157
And he was very scared of people!

40
00:02:21,791 --> 00:02:25,629
Big people, little people,
people making noise with boxes...

41
00:02:25,679 --> 00:02:26,645
how frightening!

42
00:02:26,695 --> 00:02:29,859
Boris said, hiding behind a trunk.

43
00:02:30,554 --> 00:02:35,448
He tried to hide inside an old lampshade,
but his glowing little feet stuck

44
00:02:35,498 --> 00:02:38,245
out, lighting up the whole attic.

45
00:02:39,342 --> 00:02:44,423
The next night, the wind was
blowing outside, swaying the trees.

46
00:02:44,576 --> 00:02:49,574
Suddenly, on the hallway wall,
a tiny round shadow appeared,

47
00:02:49,646 --> 00:02:51,240
and then it was gone.

48
00:02:51,883 --> 00:02:56,505
Lara took a deep breath and picked up
the flashlight from her nightstand.

49
00:02:57,117 --> 00:03:00,757
I'm a little bit scared, but I
want to find out what's up there,

50
00:03:00,807 --> 00:03:04,249
Lara said, holding the
flashlight with both hands.

51
00:03:04,854 --> 00:03:06,231
Hoo, hoo!

52
00:03:06,308 --> 00:03:09,706
Then I'm coming too, right
here on your shoulder,

53
00:03:09,756 --> 00:03:11,809
Popcorn said bravely.

54
00:03:12,495 --> 00:03:15,848
They climbed the attic stairs,
one step at a time, very,

55
00:03:15,898 --> 00:03:17,381
very slowly.

56
00:03:21,137 --> 00:03:26,051
Lara opened the attic door and shone
the flashlight into every corner.

57
00:03:26,754 --> 00:03:29,998
Who is hiding in there,
among all these old boxes?

58
00:03:30,048 --> 00:03:33,309
Lara asked, her voice trembling a little.

59
00:03:33,928 --> 00:03:38,897
Behind a trunk, a little white
glowing something jumped into the air.

60
00:03:39,567 --> 00:03:40,780
Please don't scare me!

61
00:03:41,004 --> 00:03:42,793
I'm just a teeny tiny ghost!

62
00:03:42,843 --> 00:03:45,507
Boris said, covering his eyes.

63
00:03:46,143 --> 00:03:49,918
Lara got a fright, and Boris
got an even bigger fright.

64
00:03:50,305 --> 00:03:55,246
He was so nervous that he fell
head first into a box of old socks!

65
00:03:55,892 --> 00:04:00,292
And when Boris climbed out of the box
with a striped sock hanging on his head,

66
00:04:00,419 --> 00:04:03,055
Lara couldn't stop herself from laughing.

67
00:04:03,704 --> 00:04:08,826
And Popcorn laughed so hard that
she nearly fell off Lara's shoulder.

68
00:04:09,971 --> 00:04:13,232
The two of them sat down
on the attic floor to talk.

69
00:04:13,872 --> 00:04:16,860
I'm scared of people because
you're big, you're noisy,

70
00:04:16,910 --> 00:04:19,013
and you switch on the
lights all of a sudden,

71
00:04:19,063 --> 00:04:21,602
Boris explained, still shy.

72
00:04:22,270 --> 00:04:26,424
And I'm scared of the dark because
I can't see what's inside it,

73
00:04:26,474 --> 00:04:28,874
Lara said in a small voice.

74
00:04:29,548 --> 00:04:32,781
Popcorn tilted her
little head and giggled.

75
00:04:33,374 --> 00:04:37,837
Hoo, hoo... so you two were
scared of each other all along!

76
00:04:37,887 --> 00:04:40,051
Popcorn said with a wink.

77
00:04:40,691 --> 00:04:44,660
Boris thought for a moment,
and then he began to glow,

78
00:04:44,802 --> 00:04:46,757
brighter and brighter.

79
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:54,548
The whole attic was filled
with a warm, lovely light,

80
00:04:54,598 --> 00:04:56,400
like an old lantern.

81
00:04:57,054 --> 00:04:59,696
With you here, the dark isn't dark at all!

82
00:04:59,746 --> 00:05:01,869
Lara said, amazed.

83
00:05:02,973 --> 00:05:07,581
After that, the attic became the
most fun place in the whole house.

84
00:05:08,214 --> 00:05:11,086
Boris made animal shadows on the wall:

85
00:05:11,190 --> 00:05:14,770
a bunny, an elephant, and
even a little owl with a bow.

86
00:05:15,386 --> 00:05:16,762
Hoo, hoo!

87
00:05:16,857 --> 00:05:19,756
That little owl looks exactly like me!

88
00:05:19,806 --> 00:05:23,442
Popcorn said, very pleased with herself.

89
00:05:24,133 --> 00:05:28,130
From downstairs, Lara's
mom called up the stairs.

90
00:05:28,718 --> 00:05:31,989
Lara, sweetheart, is
everything all right up there?

91
00:05:32,039 --> 00:05:34,731
Mom asked from the bottom of the stairs.

92
00:05:35,386 --> 00:05:39,278
Everything's great up here, Mom,
I'm just making a new friend!

93
00:05:39,328 --> 00:05:41,422
Lara answered with a giggle.

94
00:05:42,069 --> 00:05:46,053
Mom smiled and thought it
was just a game of pretend.

95
00:05:46,396 --> 00:05:50,088
Little did she know that the
new friend glowed in the dark!

96
00:05:51,197 --> 00:05:57,264
That night, Boris floated down,
very slowly, to Lara's bedroom.

97
00:05:57,976 --> 00:06:03,584
He hovered beside her bed and glowed
very softly, like a little night light.

98
00:06:04,219 --> 00:06:07,894
Now, when the house makes little noises,
you'll know it's just saying good

99
00:06:07,944 --> 00:06:09,055
night to us,

100
00:06:09,105 --> 00:06:11,130
Boris said with a smile.

101
00:06:11,745 --> 00:06:15,938
Good night, Boris, and thank you
so much for being my little light,

102
00:06:15,988 --> 00:06:18,735
Lara said, closing her eyes.

103
00:06:19,338 --> 00:06:24,281
Hoo, hoo... when we talk about
our fears, they get teeny tiny,

104
00:06:24,331 --> 00:06:26,843
Popcorn whispered to the stars.

105
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:32,833
And Lara slept peacefully, not scared
at all, while outside the crickets sang

106
00:06:32,883 --> 00:06:34,083
softly.

107
00:06:41,253 --> 00:06:42,453
The End.

108
00:06:44,160 --> 00:06:44,872
Hoo...

109
00:06:44,922 --> 00:06:45,946
Psst!

110
00:06:45,996 --> 00:06:47,568
Are you still awake?

111
00:06:47,722 --> 00:06:49,776
Did you like tonight's story?

112
00:06:49,884 --> 00:06:53,832
Lara and Boris showed us that
when we talk about our fears,

113
00:06:53,882 --> 00:06:58,584
they get teeny tiny, and someone who
seems different can become a wonderful

114
00:06:58,634 --> 00:06:59,800
friend.

115
00:06:59,850 --> 00:07:04,156
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

116
00:07:04,453 --> 00:07:09,350
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

117
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:11,806
for more stories at bedtime.

118
00:07:12,109 --> 00:07:13,309
Hoo...

